  "notes": {
    "addRules": {
      "fill": "orange",
      "maxH": 1100,
      "text": "How capture behaves\n\n• The shutter leaves the camera at once. Check and save opens with what was read while aiming; the sharp photo is read again behind it (about 1 s) and fills only the fields not yet touched. Save waits for that.\n\n• Cancel deletes the photo and writes nothing. Retake starts over.\n\n• The total is what is saved; the lines read are not listed. A photo of just the total is normal: the shop's field says when its name was not in the picture. Only a missing total shows \"Scan the rest\".\n\n• The amount is large with a pencil; Shop and When have one too and open in place. Tapping the photo shows it full screen, pinch to zoom.\n\n• Scan the rest joins the next photo to this one: lines both photos caught are kept once, and the two photos are stacked into one receipt, head on top, whichever was taken first.\n\n• Japanese, English and Vietnamese. A reading that looks like the wrong script is read again the other way round.\n\n• ¥, ₫/VND, $ or € on the paper (or the language) says the currency. Not the book's: Paid is in it, the rate is the last one typed, and the book gets the converted figure. \"It was in yen\" undoes a wrong guess.\n\n• Where: a place saved within 80 m first, then Apple Maps (the one thing sent off the phone), unless switched off in Your data.",
      "w": 440,
      "x": 4230,
      "y": 4400
    },
